@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5080
@apiKey = replace-with-the-secret-configured-on-your-server

### OpenAPI document. The browser UI is at {{baseUrl}}/swagger.
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json

### 1. Upload a ZIP. Change the local file path below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=deploy-boundary

--deploy-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="release.zip"
Content-Type: application/zip

< C:\Builds\release.zip
--deploy-boundary--

### 2. Deploy. Paste the actual path returned by upload.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deployments
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "zipFilePath": "C:\\IisDeployData\\uploads\\<upload-id>.zip",
  "webAppPath": "C:\\inetpub\\wwwroot\\MyApp",
  "applicationPoolName": "MyAppPool"
}

### 3. List IIS application pools, application paths, and backups.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/iis/applications
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4. Restore. Paste a real backup path from deploy or discovery.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/restores
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "backupZipPath": "C:\\IisDeployData\\backups\\<application-key>\\<backup-id>.zip",
  "webAppPath": "C:\\inetpub\\wwwroot\\MyApp",
  "applicationPoolName": "MyAppPool"
}
